# Configuration system

The typed registry in `app/config_registry.py` is the catalog of manageable
settings. Do not invent ad-hoc settings outside it.

Workflow for consequential keys: draft → validate → preview impact → test
(where applicable) → confirm → atomic apply → verify → audit. Rollback
creates a **new** revision; never mutate an applied revision.

Precedence: bootstrap/env > active global revision > registry default.
Optimistic concurrency: apply must name the expected active revision id.

Classify keys by risk (`low` / `medium` / `high` / `bootstrap`) and
editability. Bootstrap and dangerous values are read-only in the UI.
